course: dictionary
lesson: 12455
title: Defective: something with a fault
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Defective means something is not working properly because it has a fault. Look at the words around it for clues. «The toaster was defective, so it would not heat the bread.» The toaster did not work and was wrong, so defective means faulty.
explain: Shops use this word a lot. «The shop agreed to refund the defective goods.» If something you bought is broken, you can take it back and get your money back or a new one. A good check is to swap in your meaning: «faulty goods» fits the sentence, so you have understood it.
explain: In science, «a defective circuit» has a broken part, so the electricity cannot flow the right way. Defective is about a fault in a thing. It is not a word to use about people.
fact: Defective means not working properly because something is wrong with it.
fact: Defective is an adjective: «a defective part» and «defective brakes» are examples.
fact: You can say «return a defective item» when something you bought has a fault.
fact: Faulty is a close synonym for defective, and both describe a thing that does not work right.
fact: Old books sometimes used «defective» about people with disabilities, but that use is now hurtful, so never use it that way.
exercise: «The new kettle was defective and would not switch on.» What does defective mean? | Very hot | Brand new and shiny | Quiet | *Faulty, not working properly
exercise: «Please return a defective item to the shop.» What should you do with a defective item? | Keep it in a drawer forever | Hide it from the shop | Paint it a new colour | *Take it back for a replacement or refund
exercise: «The defective brakes on the bike needed fixing.» What is wrong with the brakes? | They are made of gold | They are too quiet to hear | They are very fast | *They have a fault and do not work properly
test: Which phrase describes a thing with a fault? | *a defective part | a warm breeze | a long road | a happy friend
test: Which word could replace defective in «a defective circuit»? | beautiful | hungry | sleepy | *faulty
exam: Which sentence uses defective correctly? | The defective sunset made the sky pink and gold | The defective puppy wagged its tail and ate its dinner | *The shop gave Maya a new phone because the old one was defective | Dad was defective after his long walk home
